{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016HCWJhvqxrDhKMdDhbh9Ku","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! I now have the complete picture. Here's what I found:\n\n## HumanSize API\n\n**Location:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5616/pkg/format/humansize.go`\n\n### Function Signature\n```go\nfunc HumanSize(bytes int64, opts HumanSizeOpts) string\n```\n\n### HumanSizeOpts Struct\n```go\ntype HumanSizeOpts struct {\n\tBinary bool\n}\n```\n\n### Behavior\n\nThe `HumanSize` function formats a byte count as a human-readable string with unit suffixes. Key behaviors:\n\n1. **Binary Mode** (when `opts.Binary == true`): Uses base 1024 with binary suffixes: `\"\"`, `\"K\"`, `\"M\"`, `\"G\"`, `\"T\"`, `\"P\"`, `\"E\"`\n2. **SI Mode** (when `opts.Binary == false`): Uses base 1000 with SI suffixes: `\"\"`, `\"kB\"`, `\"MB\"`, `\"GB\"`, `\"TB\"`\n3. **Formatting Rules**:\n   - Returns `\"0\"` for zero bytes\n   - At most one decimal place for fractional values (e.g., `\"1.5K\"`)\n   - No decimal place when the value is 10 or greater (e.g., `\"10K\"` not `\"10.0K\"`)\n   - Raw number (no suffix) for values less than the base unit\n\n### Test Examples\n\n**Binary mode:**\n- `512` → `\"512\"`\n- `1024` → `\"1.0K\"`\n- `1536` → `\"1.5K\"`\n- `10240` → `\"10K\"`\n- `1048576` → `\"1.0M\"`\n\n**SI mode:**\n- `500` → `\"500\"`\n- `1000` → `\"1.0kB\"`\n- `1500` → `\"1.5kB\"`\n- `1000000` → `\"1.0MB\"`"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a315170d-d3ea-4738-8b8a-db26036cb150","uuid":"d915aa74-d4bd-4c74-8a9f-769870c96cc8","timestamp":"2026-05-27T21:18:56.179Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In the repo at /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5616, find the definition of HumanSize in pkg/format/ and show me its signature and behavior. Also check if there's a HumanSizeOpts struct. I need to understand the exact API.","agentId":"af01ea35eaca96018","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! I now have the complete picture. Here's what I found:\n\n## HumanSize API\n\n**Location:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5616/pkg/format/humansize.go`\n\n### Function Signature\n```go\nfunc HumanSize(bytes int64, opts HumanSizeOpts) string\n```\n\n### HumanSizeOpts Struct\n```go\ntype HumanSizeOpts struct {\n\tBinary bool\n}\n```\n\n### Behavior\n\nThe `HumanSize` function formats a byte count as a human-readable string with unit suffixes. Key behaviors:\n\n1. **Binary Mode** (when `opts.Binary == true`): Uses base 1024 with binary suffixes: `\"\"`, `\"K\"`, `\"M\"`, `\"G\"`, `\"T\"`, `\"P\"`, `\"E\"`\n2. **SI Mode** (when `opts.Binary == false`): Uses base 1000 with SI suffixes: `\"\"`, `\"kB\"`, `\"MB\"`, `\"GB\"`, `\"TB\"`\n3. **Formatting Rules**:\n   - Returns `\"0\"` for zero bytes\n   - At most one decimal place for fractional values (e.g., `\"1.5K\"`)\n   - No decimal place when the value is 10 or greater (e.g., `\"10K\"` not `\"10.0K\"`)\n   - Raw number (no suffix) for values less than the base unit\n\n### Test Examples\n\n**Binary mode:**\n- `512` → `\"512\"`\n- `1024` → `\"1.0K\"`\n- `1536` → `\"1.5K\"`\n- `10240` → `\"10K\"`\n- `1048576` → `\"1.0M\"`\n\n**SI mode:**\n- `500` → `\"500\"`\n- `1000` → `\"1.0kB\"`\n- `1500` → `\"1.5kB\"`\n- `1000000` → `\"1.0MB\"`"}],"totalDurationMs":10370,"totalTokens":19779,"totalToolUseCount":3,"usage":{"input_tokens":5,"cache_creation_input_tokens":917,"cache_read_input_tokens":18336,"output_tokens":521,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":917},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":5,"output_tokens":521,"cache_read_input_tokens":18336,"cache_creation_input_tokens":917,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":917,"ephemeral_1